From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:05:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compare_document_order: pseudo-elements order by box position

Pseudo-element nodes carry a real `parent` but are not in that
parent's `children`, so the sibling scan at the divergence point never
found them: the loop met whichever real sibling came first and returned
an ordering as if the pseudo were on the other side (or fell through to
Equal). A `.footer::before` compared against a later real child sorted
after it.

Consumers of document order that can meet pseudo ids (the paint-order
tiebreak for re-homed abspos boxes being the first) need CSS box
order: ::before precedes all of the parent's children, ::after follows
them. Selection/Range code never passes pseudo ids, so this only makes
previously-arbitrary answers correct.

todomvc again: `.footer::before` (abspos overlay, re-homed alongside
`.filters`) sorted above `.clear-completed` and swallowed its clicks.
---
 src/traversal.rs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/traversal.rs b/src/traversal.rs
index 40c39e5..3286468 100644
--- a/src/traversal.rs
+++ b/src/traversal.rs
@@ -415,6 +415,17 @@ impl BaseDocument {
         let parent_id = chain_a[common_depth - 1];
         let parent = &self.nodes[parent_id];

+        // Pseudo-element nodes are not in parent.children, so the sibling
+        // scan below would never find them (and fell through to Equal /
+        // whichever real sibling it met first). Box order: ::before
+        // precedes all of the parent's children, ::after follows them.
+        if parent.before() == Some(divergent_a) || parent.after() == Some(divergent_b) {
+            return Ordering::Less;
+        }
+        if parent.after() == Some(divergent_a) || parent.before() == Some(divergent_b) {
+            return Ordering::Greater;
+        }
+
         for &child_id in &parent.children {
             if child_id == divergent_a {
                 return Ordering::Less;
